  "scientific_scope_status": "For a finite hidden controlled jump process with k visible labels, a repeatable hidden preparation, bounded target/probe exit rates R, a well-posed predictable visible-history controller and a frozen bounded-hazard predictor, independent random occupation time U on [0,T] defines D=E||Q^(J_U)E(X_U,:)-vhat(U,H_U)||_2^2. D has units rate squared. The source reconstructs a coupling bound TV(P_visible,P_predictor)<=min{1,delta_init+T sqrt((k-1)D)} for the entire visible path including jump times. No stationary distribution, hidden dimension, minimum label mass or training/deployment density ratio is supplied. This is an internally proved source candidate, not physical validation.",
